Z||000017||Joe Torma||07-09-2001||05:22 PM||||If you are producing a book... the print shop is going probably going to require that your images be 220-300dpi at the size of the image in the book.  So the digital images may not fly with about 72/96 dpi especially at the color depth. Also, you will probably need to convert them to CMYK for professional printing.<P>How many pages?  How much would you charge per book.<P>I own a digital printing company...if I can help, let me know.<P>Joe<p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 07-09-2001).]||||reg||1
